65,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at the options, Plan D seems great! It's on the southern side where we can hoard in stages, and it doesn't sound like it needs deep digging in the center. What do you all think?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your logic regarding the southern location is sound. However, we must consider the heat readings; a large expanse of courts could exacerbate the thermal stress. Plan A, conversely, addresses the drainage issues directly.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minato,,I like Plan A because the volunteers already enjoy habitat tasks! But I'm worried about the few workers. Would Plan D be easier for them since there are already volunteers for youth sports?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, Plan A is appealing, but my data shows that planting fails without strict aftercare. With only seven staff, the risk is too high. Plan D is more durable and aligns with the existing sports volunteers.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I share your concern. Plan A's upkeep would be triple that of hard surfaces, creating a massive budget drain. Plan D's focus on courts and seating is far more financially sustainable for the city.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I see your point about the heat, but Plan B is in the center where we can't hoard the site easily. Plan D keeps the park open and avoids the clay risks in the middle!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, you make a compelling point regarding the logistics. While Plan A is logically sound for drainage, the combination of high maintenance costs and staffing shortages makes it a precarious choice. Plan D appears the most pragmatic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I think Plan D is a good choice. It lets the sports volunteers help, and it seems like it won't be too hard for the seven workers to look after. It feels like a happy plan.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, I agree. Plan D avoids the high-risk planting of Plan C and the maintenance burden of Plan A. It is the most durable option and respects the physical constraints of the site.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. Plan D avoids the financial trap of high-maintenance greenery and leverages the southern site's accessibility. It is the only option that ensures the city isn't burdened by unsustainable costs in three years.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"It sounds like we all agree! Plan D is the safest for the ground, the easiest to build, and won't be too expensive to keep up. I'm voting for Plan D!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The logic is consistent. Plan D respects the construction constraints, avoids the financial pitfalls of high-maintenance greenery, and aligns with existing volunteer support. I shall also cast my vote for Plan D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minato,,I agree with everyone. Plan D is a kind choice because it uses the sports volunteers and won't make the few workers too tired. I vote for Plan D!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Minako,,"The evidence is clear. Plan D is the most durable and practical choice, avoiding the failures of past planting schemes and the risks of central construction. I vote for Plan D.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Plan D is the only choice that avoids the long-term financial burden of expensive upkeep while remaining practical to build. I vote for Plan D.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all found a plan we like! Plan D is definitely the way to go. Let's make this park awesome for everyone!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
81,3,4,pass,Kenji,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
82,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It has been a most productive discussion. By synthesizing our diverse concerns, we have arrived at a rational and sustainable conclusion. I am satisfied with our consensus.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
83,3,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
84,3,4,talk,Minato,,I am happy that we could all agree. I hope the people who use the sports terraces and the volunteers who help them have a wonderful time in the park.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
85,3,4,pass,Minato,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
86,3,4,talk,Minako,,I am satisfied that we have prioritized durability and practicality over mere aesthetics. Plan D is the only logical choice given the constraints. I am finished.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
87,3,4,pass,Minako,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
88,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,It has been a pleasure working with you all. I am glad we have chosen a path that ensures the city's financial peace of mind for years to come. I am finished.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
